# Build context for the bot image.
#
# Without this file `COPY . .` in bot/Dockerfile copies whatever happens to sit
# in bot/ on the host — including a node_modules directory left behind by a
# local `npm install`. That directory would land on top of the one produced by
# `npm ci` inside the image, replacing freshly resolved dependencies with stale
# ones built for a different platform. The root context already had a
# .dockerignore; the bot context did not.

# Dependencies and build output
node_modules
dist
.git

# Secrets — must never enter an image layer
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*serviceAccount*.json
*service-account*.json
*credentials*.json
*.pem
*.key

# Runtime state (lives in the mounted volume, not in the image)
data
telegram_users.json
admin_list.json
registration-requests.json

# Misc
*.log
*.bak
